{"animath": "0.1", "canvas": {"width": 960, "height": 540}, "kind": "concept", "level": "jc", "subject": "math", "topic": "h2-statistics", "title": "JC H2 statistics: sampling distributions, hypothesis testing, error types", "scenes": [{"id": "s1", "caption": "The sampling distribution of the mean shrinks as n grows", "narration": "Take the mean of a sample and repeat many times: the sample means cluster around the true mean. As the sample size n grows, the spread of those means shrinks by root n — the curve gets taller and narrower.", "duration_ms": 11000, "steps": [{"at_ms": 0, "do": "show", "shape": {"id": "xAxis", "kind": "line", "stroke": "#1a1a1a", "width": 2, "x1": 80, "y1": 450, "x2": 880, "y2": 450, "explain": "The axis of sample means: where each sample's mean lands."}}, {"at_ms": 600, "do": "show", "shape": {"id": "bell2", "kind": "polygon", "stroke": "#1a56db", "width": 3, "fill": "#dbeafe", "points": [[180.0, 447.9], [217.5, 443.6], [255.0, 432.9], [292.5, 410.7], [330.0, 372.5], [367.5, 318.4], [405.0, 257.9], [442.5, 208.9], [480.0, 190.0], [517.5, 208.9], [555.0, 257.9], [592.5, 318.4], [630.0, 372.5], [667.5, 410.7], [705.0, 432.9], [742.5, 443.6], [780.0, 447.9]], "explain": "The spread of sample means when n = 2: wide, because tiny samples vary a lot."}}, {"at_ms": 600, "do": "show", "shape": {"id": "lab2", "kind": "text", "x": 640, "y": 170, "size": 28, "text": "n = 2", "explain": "Sample size 2: the means of pairs scatter widely."}}, {"at_ms": 1600, "do": "show", "shape": {"id": "d1", "kind": "circle", "cx": 250, "cy": 300, "r": 9, "fill": "#c2410c", "explain": "One sample mean: a single dot in the scatter of means."}}, {"at_ms": 1700, "do": "show", "shape": {"id": "d2", "kind": "circle", "cx": 350, "cy": 240, "r": 9, "fill": "#c2410c", "explain": "Another sample mean: each dot is one sample's average."}}, {"at_ms": 1800, "do": "show", "shape": {"id": "d3", "kind": "circle", "cx": 480, "cy": 200, "r": 9, "fill": "#c2410c", "explain": "A sample mean near the centre: means cluster around the true mean."}}, {"at_ms": 1900, "do": "show", "shape": {"id": "d4", "kind": "circle", "cx": 620, "cy": 250, "r": 9, "fill": "#c2410c", "explain": "Another sample mean: each dot is one sample's average."}}, {"at_ms": 2000, "do": "show", "shape": {"id": "d5", "kind": "circle", "cx": 750, "cy": 310, "r": 9, "fill": "#c2410c", "explain": "One more sample mean: five draws, scattered around the centre."}}, {"at_ms": 2600, "do": "move", "target": "d1", "to": {"cx": 430, "cy": 410}, "dur_ms": 1400}, {"at_ms": 2700, "do": "move", "target": "d2", "to": {"cx": 455, "cy": 395}, "dur_ms": 1400}, {"at_ms": 2800, "do": "move", "target": "d3", "to": {"cx": 480, "cy": 405}, "dur_ms": 1400}, {"at_ms": 2900, "do": "move", "target": "d4", "to": {"cx": 505, "cy": 400}, "dur_ms": 1400}, {"at_ms": 3000, "do": "move", "target": "d5", "to": {"cx": 530, "cy": 412}, "dur_ms": 1400}, {"at_ms": 4400, "do": "show", "shape": {"id": "spread", "kind": "arrow", "stroke": "#b45309", "width": 3, "dash": "6 4", "x1": 280, "y1": 250, "x2": 680, "y2": 250, "explain": "The spread of the means for small n: wide, and shrinking as n grows."}}, {"at_ms": 5000, "do": "move", "target": "spread", "to": {"x1": 360, "x2": 600}, "dur_ms": 1200}, {"at_ms": 6200, "do": "hide", "target": "bell2"}, {"at_ms": 6200, "do": "hide", "target": "lab2"}, {"at_ms": 6200, "do": "hide", "target": "spread"}, {"at_ms": 6200, "do": "show", "shape": {"id": "bell25", "kind": "polygon", "stroke": "#1a56db", "width": 3, "fill": "#dbeafe", "points": [[330.0, 447.4], [348.8, 441.9], [367.5, 428.3], [386.2, 400.2], [405.0, 351.6], [423.8, 282.9], [442.5, 206.1], [461.2, 144.0], [480.0, 120.0], [498.8, 144.0], [517.5, 206.1], [536.2, 282.9], [555.0, 351.6], [573.8, 400.2], [592.5, 428.3], [611.2, 441.9], [630.0, 447.4]], "explain": "The same means with n = 25: taller and narrower, because larger samples vary less."}}, {"at_ms": 6200, "do": "show", "shape": {"id": "lab25", "kind": "text", "x": 640, "y": 140, "size": 28, "text": "n = 25", "explain": "Sample size 25: the means of big samples bunch up tightly."}}, {"at_ms": 6800, "do": "move", "target": "d1", "to": {"cx": 460, "cy": 418}, "dur_ms": 1200}, {"at_ms": 6900, "do": "move", "target": "d2", "to": {"cx": 470, "cy": 410}, "dur_ms": 1200}, {"at_ms": 7000, "do": "move", "target": "d3", "to": {"cx": 480, "cy": 415}, "dur_ms": 1200}, {"at_ms": 7100, "do": "move", "target": "d4", "to": {"cx": 490, "cy": 412}, "dur_ms": 1200}, {"at_ms": 7200, "do": "move", "target": "d5", "to": {"cx": 500, "cy": 420}, "dur_ms": 1200}, {"at_ms": 8400, "do": "show", "shape": {"id": "verdict", "kind": "text", "x": 260, "y": 76, "size": 28, "color": "#1f7a3a", "text": "same data, more samples → steadier mean", "explain": "The takeaway: more samples per mean gives a steadier mean."}}, {"at_ms": 9600, "do": "caption", "text": "More data, less wiggle: spread shrinks by root n"}]}, {"id": "s2", "caption": "Hypothesis testing: the p-value decides against α", "narration": "State the null and the alternative, then ask how surprising the data would be if the null were true. The p-value measures that surprise — smaller than alpha, and the null is rejected.", "duration_ms": 12000, "steps": [{"at_ms": 0, "do": "show", "shape": {"id": "h0", "kind": "latex", "x": 100, "y": 100, "size": 36, "tex": "H_{0}: \\mu = 60", "explain": "The null hypothesis: the mean is 60, the status quo we test against."}}, {"at_ms": 600, "do": "show", "shape": {"id": "h1", "kind": "latex", "x": 100, "y": 160, "size": 36, "tex": "H_{1}: \\mu > 60", "explain": "The alternative: the mean exceeds 60, what we conclude if the data is surprising."}}, {"at_ms": 1500, "do": "show", "shape": {"id": "xAxis", "kind": "line", "stroke": "#1a1a1a", "width": 2, "x1": 120, "y1": 440, "x2": 840, "y2": 440, "explain": "The test-statistic axis: the p-value is measured along it."}}, {"at_ms": 1800, "do": "show", "shape": {"id": "nullBell", "kind": "polygon", "stroke": "#1a56db", "width": 3, "fill": "#eff6ff", "points": [[180.0, 438.0], [217.5, 433.9], [255.0, 423.6], [292.5, 402.3], [330.0, 365.5], [367.5, 313.4], [405.0, 255.3], [442.5, 208.2], [480.0, 190.0], [517.5, 208.2], [555.0, 255.3], [592.5, 313.4], [630.0, 365.5], [667.5, 402.3], [705.0, 423.6], [742.5, 433.9], [780.0, 438.0]], "explain": "The null's world: the distribution of the test statistic if H0 were true."}}, {"at_ms": 1800, "do": "show", "shape": {"id": "muLab", "kind": "text", "x": 448, "y": 472, "size": 24, "text": "μ₀ = 60", "explain": "The null's centre: mu nought = 60, the claimed mean."}}, {"at_ms": 3200, "do": "show", "shape": {"id": "crit", "kind": "polygon", "fill": "#fecaca", "points": [[660.0, 396.2], [670.0, 404.1], [680.0, 410.9], [690.0, 416.7], [700.0, 421.5], [710.0, 425.5], [720.0, 428.7], [730.0, 431.3], [740.0, 433.4], [750.0, 435.0], [760.0, 436.3], [770.0, 437.3], [780.0, 438.0], [780, 440], [660, 440]], "explain": "The critical region: statistics out here are surprising enough to reject H0."}}, {"at_ms": 3200, "do": "show", "shape": {"id": "alphaLab", "kind": "latex", "x": 690, "y": 478, "size": 26, "color": "#b00020", "tex": "\\alpha = 0.05", "explain": "Alpha = 0.05: the surprise threshold; the size of the rejection region."}}, {"at_ms": 4600, "do": "show", "shape": {"id": "pRegion", "kind": "polygon", "fill": "#bbf7d0", "points": [[600.0, 324.8], [615.0, 346.2], [630.0, 365.5], [645.0, 382.2], [660.0, 396.2], [675.0, 407.7], [690.0, 416.7], [705.0, 423.6], [720.0, 428.7], [735.0, 432.4], [750.0, 435.0], [765.0, 436.8], [780.0, 438.0], [780, 440], [600, 440]], "explain": "The p-value region: statistics at least this extreme, given H0."}}, {"at_ms": 4600, "do": "show", "shape": {"id": "marker", "kind": "line", "stroke": "#b00020", "width": 4, "x1": 600, "y1": 200, "x2": 600, "y2": 440, "explain": "Our test statistic: where the observed data landed."}}, {"at_ms": 4600, "do": "show", "shape": {"id": "pLab", "kind": "latex", "x": 540, "y": 150, "size": 30, "color": "#1f7a3a", "tex": "p = 0.31", "explain": "The p-value: 0.31, far above 0.05, so H0 is not rejected."}}, {"at_ms": 6000, "do": "move", "target": "marker", "to": {"x1": 730, "x2": 730}, "dur_ms": 1200}, {"at_ms": 6000, "do": "move", "target": "pLab", "to": {"x": 668, "y": 150}, "dur_ms": 1200}, {"at_ms": 6000, "do": "hide", "target": "pRegion"}, {"at_ms": 6400, "do": "show", "shape": {"id": "pRegion2", "kind": "polygon", "fill": "#bbf7d0", "points": [[730.0, 431.3], [734.2, 432.3], [738.3, 433.1], [742.5, 433.9], [746.7, 434.5], [750.8, 435.2], [755.0, 435.7], [759.2, 436.2], [763.3, 436.7], [767.5, 437.1], [771.7, 437.4], [775.8, 437.7], [780.0, 438.0], [780, 440], [730, 440]], "explain": "The tail beyond our statistic: its area is the p-value."}}, {"at_ms": 7400, "do": "emphasize", "target": "crit"}, {"at_ms": 7400, "do": "show", "shape": {"id": "verdict", "kind": "latex", "x": 100, "y": 230, "size": 30, "color": "#b00020", "tex": "\\text{reject } H_{0}", "explain": "The verdict: the p-value fell in the rejection region, so H0 is rejected."}}, {"at_ms": 9000, "do": "caption", "text": "A rare-enough result under H₀ tips the verdict to reject"}]}, {"id": "s3", "caption": "The p-value trap: it is not P(H₀ is true)", "narration": "A p-value of 0.03 does not mean the null has a three percent chance of being true. It means: if the null were true, only three percent of experiments would give data this extreme.", "duration_ms": 10000, "steps": [{"at_ms": 0, "do": "show", "shape": {"id": "wrong", "kind": "text", "x": 120, "y": 90, "size": 32, "color": "#b00020", "text": "p = 0.03 means P(H₀ true) = 3%", "explain": "The trap: reading the p-value as the probability that H0 is true."}}, {"at_ms": 1200, "do": "show", "shape": {"id": "chip", "kind": "text", "x": 660, "y": 78, "size": 30, "color": "#b00020", "text": "3%", "explain": "The 3%: three repeats in a hundred, while H0 is true."}}, {"at_ms": 2400, "do": "show", "shape": {"id": "scena", "kind": "text", "x": 120, "y": 150, "size": 26, "text": "Repeat the test 100 times while H₀ is true:", "explain": "The correct setup: assume H0 true, then repeat the experiment 100 times."}}, {"at_ms": 3200, "do": "show", "shape": {"id": "statBell", "kind": "polygon", "stroke": "#1a56db", "width": 3, "fill": "#eff6ff", "points": [[150.0, 458.6], [191.2, 455.6], [232.5, 448.2], [273.8, 432.8], [315.0, 406.3], [356.2, 368.9], [397.5, 327.0], [438.8, 293.1], [480.0, 280.0], [521.2, 293.1], [562.5, 327.0], [603.8, 368.9], [645.0, 406.3], [686.2, 432.8], [727.5, 448.2], [768.8, 455.6], [810.0, 458.6]], "explain": "The null distribution: what the test statistic does when H0 is true."}}, {"at_ms": 3600, "do": "show", "shape": {"id": "tailShade", "kind": "polygon", "fill": "#fde68a", "points": [[640.0, 402.3], [654.2, 413.3], [668.3, 422.8], [682.5, 430.9], [696.7, 437.7], [710.8, 443.1], [725.0, 447.5], [739.2, 450.9], [753.3, 453.5], [767.5, 455.4], [781.7, 456.8], [795.8, 457.9], [810.0, 458.6], [810, 460], [640, 460]], "explain": "The tail: the 3% of repeats whose statistics land this far out."}}, {"at_ms": 3600, "do": "show", "shape": {"id": "tailLab", "kind": "text", "x": 560, "y": 120, "size": 24, "text": "3% of repeats land out here", "explain": "3% of repeats land in the tail: that is all the p-value says."}}, {"at_ms": 5000, "do": "move", "target": "chip", "to": {"x": 700, "y": 410}, "dur_ms": 1000}, {"at_ms": 6200, "do": "hide", "target": "wrong"}, {"at_ms": 6200, "do": "hide", "target": "chip"}, {"at_ms": 6200, "do": "show", "shape": {"id": "right", "kind": "latex", "x": 120, "y": 300, "size": 30, "color": "#1f7a3a", "tex": "p = P\\left(\\text{data this extreme} \\mid H_{0} \\text{ true}\\right)", "explain": "The right reading: the p-value is P(data this extreme GIVEN H0 is true)."}}, {"at_ms": 7400, "do": "emphasize", "target": "right"}, {"at_ms": 8600, "do": "caption", "text": "The p-value is about the data, not the hypothesis"}]}, {"id": "s4", "caption": "Type I and Type II errors: the two ways to be wrong", "narration": "A hypothesis test can go wrong in two ways. A Type I error rejects a true null — a false alarm, capped by alpha; a Type II error accepts a false null — a missed signal, fought with power.", "duration_ms": 11000, "steps": [{"at_ms": 0, "do": "show", "shape": {"id": "frame", "kind": "rect", "x": 180, "y": 90, "w": 600, "h": 360, "stroke": "#1a1a1a", "width": 2, "explain": "The error table: reality across the top, our decision down the side."}}, {"at_ms": 0, "do": "show", "shape": {"id": "vline", "kind": "line", "stroke": "#1a1a1a", "width": 2, "x1": 480, "y1": 90, "x2": 480, "y2": 450, "explain": "The divider between the two realities: H0 true on the left, H0 false on the right."}}, {"at_ms": 0, "do": "show", "shape": {"id": "hline", "kind": "line", "stroke": "#1a1a1a", "width": 2, "x1": 180, "y1": 270, "x2": 780, "y2": 270, "explain": "The divider between our two decisions: reject H0 above, accept H0 below."}}, {"at_ms": 0, "do": "show", "shape": {"id": "colH0", "kind": "text", "x": 290, "y": 62, "size": 26, "text": "H₀ true", "explain": "Reality column one: the null is actually true."}}, {"at_ms": 0, "do": "show", "shape": {"id": "colH1", "kind": "text", "x": 590, "y": 62, "size": 26, "text": "H₀ false", "explain": "Reality column two: the null is actually false."}}, {"at_ms": 0, "do": "show", "shape": {"id": "rowRej", "kind": "text", "x": 40, "y": 190, "size": 26, "text": "Reject H₀", "explain": "Decision row one: we reject the null."}}, {"at_ms": 0, "do": "show", "shape": {"id": "rowAcc", "kind": "text", "x": 40, "y": 370, "size": 26, "text": "Accept H₀", "explain": "Decision row two: we do not reject the null."}}, {"at_ms": 2000, "do": "show", "shape": {"id": "marker", "kind": "circle", "cx": 250, "cy": 180, "r": 10, "fill": "#b00020", "explain": "The marker: this scenario lands in the Type I cell - rejecting a true null."}}, {"at_ms": 2600, "do": "show", "shape": {"id": "t1shade", "kind": "rect", "x": 180, "y": 90, "w": 300, "h": 180, "fill": "#fecaca", "explain": "The false-alarm cell: H0 true, but we rejected it."}}, {"at_ms": 2800, "do": "show", "shape": {"id": "cellT1", "kind": "text", "x": 320, "y": 165, "size": 28, "color": "#b00020", "text": "Type I", "explain": "Type I error: rejecting a true null."}}, {"at_ms": 3000, "do": "show", "shape": {"id": "cellT1s", "kind": "text", "x": 305, "y": 205, "size": 22, "color": "#7f1d1d", "text": "false alarm", "explain": "A false alarm: the test cried wolf."}}, {"at_ms": 3200, "do": "show", "shape": {"id": "cellT1a", "kind": "latex", "x": 330, "y": 240, "size": 24, "color": "#b00020", "tex": "P = \\alpha", "explain": "Its probability: alpha, the rate we cap in advance."}}, {"at_ms": 5200, "do": "move", "target": "marker", "to": {"cx": 640, "cy": 300}, "dur_ms": 1400}, {"at_ms": 6200, "do": "show", "shape": {"id": "t2shade", "kind": "rect", "x": 480, "y": 270, "w": 300, "h": 180, "fill": "#fde68a", "explain": "The missed-signal cell: H0 false, but we accepted it."}}, {"at_ms": 6400, "do": "show", "shape": {"id": "cellT2", "kind": "text", "x": 600, "y": 340, "size": 28, "color": "#92400e", "text": "Type II", "explain": "Type II error: accepting a false null."}}, {"at_ms": 6600, "do": "show", "shape": {"id": "cellT2s", "kind": "text", "x": 552, "y": 380, "size": 22, "color": "#78350f", "text": "missed signal", "explain": "A missed signal: the real effect slipped past the test."}}, {"at_ms": 6800, "do": "show", "shape": {"id": "cellT2b", "kind": "latex", "x": 600, "y": 416, "size": 24, "color": "#92400e", "tex": "P = \\beta", "explain": "Its probability: beta, fought with bigger samples and more power."}}, {"at_ms": 7800, "do": "show", "shape": {"id": "corr1", "kind": "text", "x": 290, "y": 360, "size": 26, "color": "#1f7a3a", "text": "✓ correct", "explain": "A correct call: H0 true and we accepted it."}}, {"at_ms": 7800, "do": "show", "shape": {"id": "power", "kind": "latex", "x": 585, "y": 165, "size": 24, "color": "#1f7a3a", "tex": "\\text{Power } = 1-\\beta", "explain": "Power: 1 minus beta, the chance of catching a real effect."}}, {"at_ms": 9600, "do": "caption", "text": "α caps Type I errors; power fights Type II"}]}]}